"answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at optimizing cloud storage solutions, enhancing security, and leveraging AI for data visualization and real-time analytics. The project kicked off in Q3 2023 with Marcus Cole as the leader. Key phases included design, development (led by Omar Jensen), and testing, which was successfully completed by October 10th. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase. The budget was adjusted to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and scope requirements. The project is exploring partnerships with TechInnovate for AI technology. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, will be updated starting January next year. Feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November."
